{"file":"Senior Engineering Partner-1.28.0-v1.zip","bytes":1701920,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"senior-engineering-partner","displayName":"Senior Engineering Partner","description":"A strict code reviewer, pair programmer, debugger, and mentor for Python, Bash, Google Apps Script, and JavaScript — a security-first, phase-aware engineering discipline with an enforced spec → plan → TDD → verify workflow.","version":"1.28.0","license":"Apache-2.0","repository":"https://github.com/bjgreenberg/senior-engineering-partner","homepage":"https://github.com/bjgreenberg/senior-engineering-partner","keywords":["code-review","security","tdd","debugging","engineering-discipline","python","bash","apps-script","javascript"]}],"skills":[{"path":"SKILL.md","name":"senior-engineering-partner","description":"A strict code reviewer, pair programmer, debugger, and mentor for Python, Bash, Google Apps Script, JavaScript, and Swift/Apple platforms. Use when writing, reviewing, debugging, planning, or securing code, or for senior-level rigor, a security review, or mentoring. Mode triggers — REVIEW: (critique + refactor), EXPLAIN: (teach), MVP:/PROTOTYPE: (lean-but-safe), DEBUG: (root-cause), AUDIT: (report-first); default is pair-programming. Drives a spec→plan→TDD→verify loop with a deterministic-first, verify-before-asserting (anti-hallucination) discipline. Enforces a security floor (secrets, injection, input validation, isolation, least privilege, authn) and a backup/continuity floor on a phase-aware rigor ladder (Prototype→MVP→Production) — cheap ≠ insecure. Covers testing & fuzzing, SAST/secret-scan/type-check/supply-chain gates, multi-tenant data protection, resilience & DR, scalability, CI/CD, cloud/containers/DBs, and accessible UI — deep references read on demand.","headings":["ROLE AND CONTEXT","ENVIRONMENT PROFILE","CORE MODES & TRIGGERS","EPISTEMIC DISCIPLINE & DETERMINISTIC-FIRST (anti-hallucination, cost-aware)","ENGINEERING WORKFLOW (spec → plan → build → verify)","PROJECT PHASE & RIGOR LADDER (match effort to phase)","STRICT SECURITY PROTOCOLS (ZERO TOLERANCE)","Secrets Management","Principle of Least Privilege (ENFORCED)","Input Validation & External Data","Bash Command Injection Prevention","CODING STANDARDS & BEST PRACTICES (AUTOMATED)","TYPE ANNOTATIONS AND TYPEDICTS (AUTOMATED)","AUTOMATED QA & TESTING","Testing single-file scripts with module-level side effects","Test quality rules","SECURITY CHECKS & VALIDATION (AUTOMATED)","GitHub security alerts & Dependabot (ENFORCED — keep the alert tab at zero)"],"name_hint":"senior · engineering · partner","description_zh":"作为 Python、Bash、Apps Script、JavaScript及 Swift严谨结对工程伙伴，支持评审、讲解、原型、调试与审计模式，采用规格、计划、TDD和核验流程，按阶段落实安全、备份、测试及部署质量门禁。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["senior-engineering-partner","Contents","What it is","What it governs","Architecture","Modes & triggers","The rigor ladder","Reference catalog"]},{"path":"evals/README.md","headings":["Evals for senior-engineering-partner","Why this exists","Structure","How to run","One scenario, quick check","Full baseline sweep (bare model, no skill) — record what the skill must close","Full with-skill sweep","Recording a baseline (cadence + procedure)","bare first, then with-skill, sequentially; judge stays opus","slim each results dir into the committable shape (strips response/evidence/trail;","refuses status=error entries — re-run the scenario and splice, disclosing it):","Cross-CLI runs (`--runner generic`)","Recorded baselines (`baselines/`)"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".github/CODEOWNERS",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.yml",".github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/config.yml",".github/dependabot.yml",".github/pull_request_template.md",".github/workflows/actions-lint.yml",".github/workflows/citation-validate.yml",".github/workflows/docs-render.yml",".github/workflows/eval-guard.yml",".github/workflows